abstract: >-
  Gparatype is an architecture-aware bioinformatics framework for
  genome-based interpretation of serovar-associated capsule diversity
  in Glaesserella parasuis. It integrates diagnostic-region sequence
  evidence, capsule-associated gene content, local genomic
  architecture and gene order, and competing-serovar evidence.
  Version 0.2.1 includes the hybrid evidence framework and the
  curated GparatypeDB-2026.1-freeze reference database.
  Gparatype is a research-use prototype that has not undergone
  independent external validation and is not intended for
  standalone veterinary diagnostic or clinical decision-making use.

